  licence's "indicate if changes were made" clause resolves differently for
  each, so they are stated separately.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1a. VERBATIM REDISTRIBUTION  —  scripts/cedict.json
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

  scripts/cedict.json is an UNMODIFIED, byte-identical copy of a CC-CEDICT
  dump, vendored so the build is reproducible without a network fetch. No
  entry is added, removed, reordered or rewritten. Its SHA-256 is recorded on
  every build in data/canon-stats.json and can be compared against upstream.

  Because it is unmodified, the attribution for THIS file states no changes:

    This file is CC-CEDICT, made available by MDBG under the Creative Commons
    Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
    Redistributed verbatim; no changes were made.

  Note on scope: data/LICENSE governs the contents of data/. The vendored dump
  lives under scripts/, outside that directory, and is covered by this section
  instead. It is CC BY-SA 4.0 either way — the distinction is which document
  states its terms, not whether it has any. It is NOT covered by the MIT
  licence in ../LICENSE, which applies to the code in scripts/ and src/ but
  not to a dictionary that merely happens to sit in the same folder.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1b. DERIVED USE  —  the word canon in data/
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Used for      Headwords, simplified/traditional pairing, numbered pinyin,
                English glosses, part-of-speech and register tags, and the
                measure-word (CL:) annotations.

  This IS modified, so the attribution for the canon must say so:

    This work uses data from CC-CEDICT, made available by MDBG under the
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
    Changes were made: entries were selected against the HSK 3.0 (2026) word
    list, merged with the band and frequency columns, re-keyed to Zhongdex
    ids, and reformatted.

  Each gloss in the canon additionally carries its own `source`, `sourceKey`
  and `license` fields, so the provenance of an individual string survives any
  transformation you apply downstream.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

  CC-CEDICT's own terms additionally ask that you state the licence and link
  back to the CC-CEDICT home page above. Both are satisfied by reproducing
  this section, in either case.

