4. HSK 3.0 (2026) word list  —  IN THIS BUILD
================================================================================

  Source        Vendored at scripts/hsk30.csv.
  Licence       UNRESOLVED — see the open item below.
  Used for      The HSK 3.0 (2026) band assignment, and the traditional forms,
                pinyin and part-of-speech tags that come with it. Every canon
                record carries the upstream row id (hsk.listId, e.g. L1-0427)
                and a `hsk30:<row id>` entry in sourceIds, so any band
                assignment traces back to its exact upstream line.
  Integrity     data/canon-stats.json records the SHA-256 of the vendored file
                on every build, so a change to it is visible in the diff.

  OPEN ITEM, and this file will not claim otherwise. The vendored CSV carries
  no upstream header, no licence text and no commit reference, so this
  repository cannot currently name its provenance with confidence. The program
  plan's intent is to pin `drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary`
  (https://github.com/drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary, MIT) at a specific
  commit; that pinning has not been done, and the vendored file's header does
  not match that project's published format.

  Until it is pinned:
    * do not assert an upstream or a licence for this file that has not been
      verified, here or anywhere else;
    * if it is MIT, MIT's copyright and permission notice must travel with it,
      and that notice must be added to this section and to the file itself;
    * whoever pins it records the source URL and commit SHA in this section in
      the same commit.

  Note on counts: this repository's pinned snapshot contains 11,092 rows split
  500 / 772 / 973 / 1,000 / 1,071 / 1,140 / 5,636 across levels 1-6 and the
  combined 7-9 band. Other vintages of the HSK 3.0 list circulate with
  different totals. The contract eval asserts against the pinned snapshot, so
  a silent upstream change fails CI rather than shipping.

